WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.100
If your prep is MiraLAX, this video will walk you through exactly how to take

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:04.240
it.

3
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:09.360
Just follow along step by step. For this prep, you'll need a few items,

4
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:14.400
all available over the counter, no prescription needed. You'll need one 238-gram

5
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.120
bottle of

6
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:20.300
MiraLAX powder, two to four Dulcolax laxative tablets, and 64 ounces of a clear

7
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:20.880
sports drink

8
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.890
like Gatorade Propel or Crystal Light. That's usually two 32-ounce bottles. If you

9
00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:26.800
have diabetes,

10
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.830
use sugar-free Gatorade G2. Also, make sure you get the laxative tablets, not

11
00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:32.720
the stool softener.

12
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.280
One important rule, your sports drink cannot be red, orange, blue, or purple.

13
00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:43.400
Stick to clear or light-colored flavors. The day before your colonoscopy, you

14
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.320
'll start by mixing

15
00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:49.310
the solution. Pour the entire bottle of MiraLAX into a pitcher with all 64

16
00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:50.320
ounces of the sports

17
00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:54.800
drink. Stir or shake until the powder is completely dissolved. You can chill it

18
00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:55.600
in the refrigerator

19
00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:59.840
if you'd like. Keeping it cold makes it easier to drink. Now for part one.

20
00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:04.800
The evening before your procedure. At four p.m., take your Dulcolax tablets

21
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:05.920
with a glass of water.

22
00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:09.600
Your doctor's instructions will tell you whether to take two or four. Follow

23
00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:10.480
their guidance on the

24
00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:14.160
specific amount. At five p.m., you'll start drinking the first half of the

25
00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.400
solution. That's 32 ounces.

26
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.420
Drink an eight ounce glass every 15 minutes until that half is gone. Keep

27
00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:22.000
drinking clear liquids

28
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.200
after you finish. For part two, six hours before your colonoscopy, you'll drink

29
00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.080
the second half,

30
00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:32.980
which is another 32 ounces. Drink this at the same pace, an eight ounce glass

31
00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:33.840
every 15 minutes.

32
00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.670
You can continue to have clear liquids up until four hours before your

33
00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:38.560
procedure.

34
00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:43.520
This part is really important. You must drink all of the prep solution as

35
00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:43.760
directed,

36
00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:47.750
even if you're already passing clear liquid. I know it can feel like enough,

37
00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:48.320
but finishing the

38
00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:52.070
entire dose is what gives us the clearest view during your procedure. If the

39
00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:53.680
prep isn't completed as

40
00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:58.590
directed, we may need to reschedule, and neither of us wants that. Please drink

41
00:01:58.590 --> 00:01:59.280
plenty of liquids

42
00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:03.280
throughout the process to prevent dehydration. Staying hydrated will help you

43
00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:04.080
feel better and

44
00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:08.720
help the prep do its job. If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips

45
00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:10.080
to the bathroom,

46
00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:15.040
applying a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash cream can really help. That

47
00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:17.040
's it. You've got this.

48
00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:23.120
Follow the timing. Finish the full dose and stay hydrated. If you have any

49
00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:23.920
questions at all,

50
00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:27.360
don't hesitate to call our office. We're here to help.
